  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposals would result in substantial harm to the architectural and historic significance of a Locally Listed building and fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Wimbledon North Conservation Area. There are no public benefits to outweigh this loss and harm. As such, the proposals are considered to fail to comply with Policy D12.5 of Merton's Local Plan 2024-2037/8, Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021 and Chapter 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024). ",
    "Reason : 2 - During the application process Climate Change Officers requested more information in order to assess the energy efficiency of the proposed dwelling. This information was not forthcoming. As such, the proposals are considered to fail to comply with Policies CC2.5 and CC2.6 of Merton's Local Plan 2024-2037/8.",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure the self-build or custom-build exemption in relation to Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG), the proposed development fails to demonstrate compliance with the requirements of the Environment Act 2021. Without such an agreement, the application does not provide adequate certainty that the development qualifies for exemption from BNG obligations. As such, the proposal is contrary to the Environment Act 2021 and Merton Local Plan Policy O15.3.",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of a legal agreement securing a carbon offset contribution, the application fails to demonstrate compliance with the Mayor's net-zero carbon target contrary to Merton Local Plan Policy CC2.2",
    "Reason : 5 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe applicant/agent was informed of information missing s arising during the application and how these could potentially be overcome but sufficient information was not forthcoming. \r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n\"\t\r\n"
  ],
